  "question": {
    "text": "Diamond has a three dimensional structure of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> atoms formed by covalent bonds. The structure of diamond has face centred cubic lattice where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the tetrahedral voids are also occupied by carbon atoms. The number of carbon atoms present per unit cell of diamond is ________.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "8",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Carbon atoms occupy FCC lattice points as well as half of the tetrahedral voids</p><p>therefore number of carbon atoms atoms per unit cell <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
